chapter BRIDGITTE_REPORT_BACK:
    narrator "Bridgitte is outside her house, tightening a leather wrap around a practice post."
    narrator "She looks up as you approach, then studies you for a long beat."

    bridgitte "You're back."

    player "The coyote is dead."

    bridgitte "I know."
    bridgitte "You came back straighter."
    bridgitte "That happens when fear gets used and not obeyed."

    player "It still felt ugly."

    bridgitte "Most real fights do."
    bridgitte "That does not make the work less necessary."

    player "So what now?"

    bridgitte "Now you stop pretending an adventurer's life is only monsters."
    bridgitte "You need hands that can gather, eyes that can notice, and enough patience to respect the tools keeping you alive."

    bridgitte "If you want quicker hands, ask around in the tavern about five finger fillet."
    bridgitte "Foolish game. Useful lesson."

    bridgitte "If you want foundation, go mine brittle copper and then visit Lydia at the smithy."
    bridgitte "Bring ten pieces."
    bridgitte "She respects effort more than introductions."

    bridgitte "If you want coin, gather ten medicine herbs and ten flax for the shopkeep."
    bridgitte "The shop is not ready to deal with you yet, but the work itself is."

    bridgitte "And if you want to keep hunting, the forest edge has more than one coyote in it."
    bridgitte "The next one will not be the same lesson twice."

    player "What do you recommend first?"

    bridgitte "Lydia."
    bridgitte "Copper first. Smithy second."
    bridgitte "Learn what a blade is before you trust one with your life."

    call resolveQuestStep("cull_arkama_coyote", "report_back_to_bridgitte")
    call startQuest("learn_five_finger_fillet")
    call startQuest("lydia_smithing_intro")
    call startQuest("shopkeep_forest_supplies")

    bridgitte "Go on, then."
    bridgitte "You survived the loud lesson."
    bridgitte "Now start learning the quieter ones."
